# T265. Convoke's own repository tooling that `files[]` would otherwise ship, because it carries
# `scripts/` whole. Nothing an operator runs reaches these: no `bin`, not `index.js`, not
# `postinstall`, not a migration. Several do harm in an operator's project rather than nothing --
# `archive.js --apply` rewrites the tree it is run in, and `convoke-check.js` starts linting it.
#
# The list is kept honest by `tests/lib/shipped-scripts-reachable.test.js`, which walks the require
# graph from every entry point and fails if a shipped script is unreachable (add it here) or a
# reachable one is missing from the package (take it out of here). Same mechanism and reasoning as
# `scripts/audit/.npmignore` (T257): not a `!` negation in `files[]`, which must stay free of glob
# metacharacters (dist-2.3a).
#
# Paths start with `/` so each matches only its own location under scripts/, not a file of the same
# name in another directory.

/archive.js
/convoke-check.js
/docs-audit.js
/generate-manifest.js
/test-runner.js
/lib/t66-gate.js
/lib/types.js
/portability/catalog-generator.js
/portability/classify-skills.js
/portability/seed-catalog-repo.js
/portability/test-constants.js
/portability/validate-classification.js
/portability/validate-exports.js
